  description: 'Constable Bambis the first was said to have been a childhood friend
    of the afformationed mage. Upon his return to the city, he saw the mage''s wrath.
    He pleaded with his old friend, to let the townfolk go, the circumstanced that
    led them to this point were not their fault. However, the mage could not be reasoned
    with..


    The mage had decided, that those not worthy knowledge, were not
    worthy of their life. Every man woman or child whose answer did not please him,
    would face the most utterly brutal death of being burnt alive.'
